  "review": { "authority": "first_party_published", "method": "dual_reviewer", "reviewers": [{ "id": "spec-registry-rebuild-lane-20260819", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-19" }, { "id": "normalization-review-20260829", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-29" }], "notes": "Normalized from the 2026-08-19 rebuild research, and scoped deliberately to State's own form. State runs a second application channel at statemgmt.getsnapcast.com/become-a-model that its own site never links to, and it is a different application: 3MB enforced per file, an accept list without HEIC, an account created inside the form, and Snapcast's terms rather than State's - including a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide licence to the applicant's likeness. That channel is not published here as a series because this schema carries one channel per revision and the authored brief already sets the two side by side; it should get its own series and its own brief rather than inherit this one. No mime rule is asserted for this form: image/* with HEIC and HEIF named is a wildcard rather than a format list, so it is recorded as an ambiguous unknown and an export defaults to JPEG. The absence of a size cap here is recorded as unpublished, not as unlimited, and the unknown names the contrast with the Snapcast channel so neither number is read onto the other. The photo instruction is written as encouragement, so its four rules carry the encouraged modality rather than required. Two facts about State's own pages are recorded here rather than in the rules: the terms the form asks an applicant to accept are booking conditions written for clients, and the privacy policy gives two different addresses for the same office." }
